-- A regression guard for the amended *Deferred receiver* rule
-- (static-dispatch-spike.md §11, 2026-09-26; checker-v2.md §10.8): the
-- half that still refuses. `f`'s `x.combine n` is a method constraint on its
-- own group's `x`, generalised into `f`'s scheme (`where a.combine`); `g` is
-- in no group with `f`, so its record meets an instantiated requirement,
-- which has no field accessor to be: `no_methods_on_shape` at `f n { … }`.
-- The recursive twin, where `f` calls `g` back and the
-- record reaches `f` before it is generalised, is accepted:
-- `tests/corpus/run/DeferredReceiverRecursiveTwin.beni`.
f n x = x.combine n


g n =
    if n > 5 then
        n
    else
        f n { combine = λz → z + 1 }
